        "aspect": 1.347
      },
      "tags": [
        "paintings",
        "selected"
      ],
      "description": "This work forms part of an ongoing series exploring the bed as a site of intimacy and vulnerability. The series began after finding a photograph of my father in bed in a family photo album, taken during a period of depression that he later wrote about in his memoir. Around the same time, I saw Tracey Emin’s My Bed at the Tate.The bed is a humanising site- one in which people's most private and universal selves emerge. I find that painting people in beds dissolves distinctions of difference for me. There is a way in which I feel able to touch, even partially, some fresh and human core that can get hidden in leathered outer layers."
    },
